course: dictionary
lesson: 13205
title: Fundraise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To fundraise means to collect money for a charity, a school or a good cause. People often do it by holding events, such as a bake sale or a sponsored walk.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Our class wants to fundraise for the animal shelter, so we are holding a cake sale on Friday.» The animal shelter and the cake sale tell you that fundraise means collecting money for a good cause.
explain: Fundraise is a verb, so it changes: fundraises, fundraised, fundraising. A person who runs a fundraising event is a fundraiser. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "Our class wants to collect money for the animal shelter" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: To fundraise means to collect money for a charity, a school or a good cause.
fact: You can also fundraise by asking people or organisations to give money to support a project.
fact: Common fundraisers include bake sales, sponsored walks, fun runs, raffles and non-uniform days.
fact: The forms are fundraise, fundraises, fundraised and fundraising; a fundraiser is a person or event that raises money.
fact: Useful phrases are fundraise for charity, a fundraising event and reach the target.
exercise: «Our school will fundraise for the hospital by holding a sponsored walk.» What does fundraise mean here? | To ask for a day off | *To collect money for a good cause | To build a new school | To cook lunch for everyone
exercise: Which word is the noun for a person who raises money for a cause? | fundraising | *fundraiser | fundraised | fundraises
exercise: «Ella's class needs £300 to reach the target, and they have raised £180.» How much more money do they need? | £480 | *£120 | £90 | £180
test: «The children fundraised by holding a non-uniform day and raised £75.» What did the children do to raise money? | *Held a non-uniform day | Went on a school trip | Wrote a story | Did a spelling test
test: Which phrase means to reach the amount of money you aimed for? | Lose the raffle | *Reach the target | Ask the teacher | Miss the bus
exam: «Our club wants to fundraise for the animal rescue centre, so the members are running a fun run and selling raffle tickets.» Which of these is a fundraising activity from the text? | *Running a fun run | Reading a map | Painting the classroom | Visiting the library
